<title>RUSSIA: Russian 96 gold output up slightly to 124 T-agency.</title>
<headline>Russian 96 gold output up slightly to 124 T-agency.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian gold output in 1996 was 124 tonnes, up slightly from 1995's 122 tonnes, Prime-Tass news agency quoted an Industry Ministry official as saying on Friday.</p>
<p>It quoted Vladimir Piskunov, head of the ministry's precious metals and stones department, as also saying that 1997 gold output was targeted at 140 tonnes, but that a financing crisis could reduce the actual result by as much as 50 percent.</p>
</text>
